  "solution": {
    "text": "Vitamin K refers to structurally similar, fat-soluble vitamins&nbsp;found in foods and marketed as dietary supplements. The human body requires vitamin K for post-synthesis modification of certain proteins that are required for blood coagulation or for controlling binding of calcium in bones and other tissues. Due to deficiency of vitamin K&nbsp;causes increases in blood clotting time.",
